FerrionOS change to the upstream installer (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 16d39fe1f20f15fc97fa3aaa216ac7e449637d41 after ferrion-live-disk.patch, ferrion-install-recovery.patch and ferrion-install-clear-ring.patch (issue 7). The file-copy install works on a FerrionOS live system:
- the text and graphical installers list the files to copy from the package heads in var/lib/packages and the repository key in etc/pkg/id_ed25519.pub.toml, where the package manager keeps them, instead of a pkg directory that a FerrionOS root does not have.
- when a file the configuration wrote is also a package file (/etc/hosts, say), the live system's copy replaces it, as the image build left it; before, the copy stopped with "File exists".
- with_redoxfs_mount ends its mount by stopping the mount loop and removing the scheme from the process's namespace through the namespace manager. redoxfs::unmount_path removes /scheme/<name> through the mounted scheme itself, which the installer's redoxfs answers with EOPNOTSUPP, and that error used to hide the install's own error.

